  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.0.13\n- Citations are compared span by span: refresh and reconcile sort each fact into untouched, stale, or unconfirmed, fall back to watching the whole file when a locator cannot be resolved, and digest after normalizing line endings and trailing whitespace. reconcile --dry-run reports alreadyStale apart from untouched; doctor reports knowledge.source.changed, knowledge.observation.stale, and knowledge.observation.unconfirmed.\n- A human who did not write a stale or unconfirmed fact can confirm that it still holds (knowledge observation confirm; MCP confirm_knowledge_observation): citations are re-bound, id, history, and trace are kept, and the fact returns to accepted or to proposed. A cited source from another repository is refused.\n- Proposed observations are routed to an explainable review role and can be delegated with an audit trail; stale and unconfirmed facts appear in the role queue with a confirm action and their citation.\n- New knowledge queue --role (with --lifecycle defaulting to the single project) and MCP review_queue and validate_knowledge.\n- MCP: server name octoevidence, --mode full|knowledge (knowledge registers no review, approve, or project-mutation tool), --actor-policy any|agent-only (refuses human: actors), an explicit actor on every mutating tool with rationale on revise and trace, and renamed tools generate_feature_document, list_feature_documents, new_id, setup_agents, list_agent_roles, and create_agent_prompt.\n- Portal: loopback only with a refusal to start elsewhere, a per-process API token, Host validation, compressed responses, queue counts of actionable decisions only, citations in the queue, decision dialogs that say who decides and that a decision is recorded once, a six-step task.state glyph, and a map that folds repeated facts and files into references.\n- Records are written with LF line endings on every OS and document currency is line-ending independent. source add, source refresh, and lifecycle reconcile default --revision to a clean work tree's HEAD and record the acting --actor as updatedBy.\n- planned to approved requires the task's story to be accepted and four eyes (the approver authored neither the story nor the change); a rejected record must be revised before it can be accepted.\n- Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 usage error, 2 refusal, 3 doctor unhealthy or agent setup incomplete, 4 unexpected (message only). Role aliases solution-architect and sa. A residual risk is stated in the record that carries it and accepted with that record; there is no separate risk surface.",
